                                 Production

                              What does it do?

This door deletes file from a directory and changes in dirn that you
have deleted the file. You can choose between a semiautomatic mode where
you answer questions (ex [D]elete [M]ove or [S]kip file?). Or an automatic
mode where it deletes from one date to another.


                                    Why?

Coz I needed one and I couldn't find any door that came up to my special
demands. Of course I made it in C to accomplish some speed.


                                 Disclaimer

I don't take any responsibility for any damage this door make on your
computer hardware or software. It has been fully tested so it shouldn't
give ya any problems. Remember that this door deletes files so test it
with care until you now exactly how it works.


                                Installation

-Copy the file BBS/Doors/Deletefiles/Deletefiles to Doors:Deletefiles/ (or
 wherever you keep your doors)


                                  /X 2.xx

-Modify your custom-commands and add the following line:

*Delete   XM2550Doors:Deletefiles/Deletefiles

^         ^     ^
|         |     |_ Or wherever you put Deletefiles.
|         |
|         |___ Notice the "X" Deletefiles is an XIM door!
|
|______ The name to run.

                                  /X 3.xx

-Copy the icon BBS/Commands/BBsCmd/Delete.info to BBS/Commands/BBsCmd/ or
 BBS/Commands/SysCmd/ if u don't want that "Deletefiles" can be chosen
 from the prompt.


                                 Tooltypes

-----------------------------------------+
DIR_PATH=bbs:conf1.elite/dir1            }----+
-----------------------------------------+    |
This tooltype must have the path to the       |
file containing the filelist.              <--+

-----------------------------------------+
UPLOAD_PATH=bbs:conf1.elite/upload       }----+
-----------------------------------------+    |
This tooltype must have the path to the       |
directory where the files in the filelist  <--+
are defined.

------------------------------------------+
MOVE_PATH=work:temp                       }----+
------------------------------------------+    |
This tooltype must have the path to the        |
directory where the files will be moved.    <--+

It's very important that you get these Tooltypes right. Deletefiles 1.0 is
dezigned to delete files!


